{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1772836376313,"sessionID":"ses_33ab7ce6cffeKY4KUUDy0n9FCY","part":{"id":"prt_cc5484db1001JrZvU8aEY98fa3","sessionID":"ses_33ab7ce6cffeKY4KUUDy0n9FCY","messageID":"msg_cc548326c001UhNohFWcXGzNyv","type":"tool","callID":"call_function_cxtix2s1qly3_1","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/paule/MAD/.tmp/add-code-path-to-board.instructions"},"output":"<path>/home/paule/MAD/.tmp/add-code-path-to-board.instructions</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>1: # Design Planning: add code path to board\n2: \n3: **Description:** Add a code path and context file to each board's configuration so that AI agents know where the associated project code lives and have access to project-level context whenever they are invoked. A board lives inside the project it represents (e.g., ~/mycode/.mad/boards/myboard), so the root code path is derivable, but it should be made explicit. Two additions: (1) a `code_path` field in ~/.mad/config.json pointing to the project root, and (2) a ~/.mad/CONTEXT.md file for free-form project context. Agents should also be started with their working directory set to the project root, not the individual work item directory. Every time an agent is invoked, its instructions should include the code path and the path to CONTEXT.md at the top.\n4: \n5: ---\n6: \n7: You are an AI helping plan this feature. Generate a plan based on the description.\n8: \n9: **Your task:**\n10: 1. Analyze the feature description\n11: 2. Identify any unclear points or areas needing clarification\n12: 3. If you have questions for the human, list them in a JSON array under \"questions\"\n13: 4. If you have enough info, write a complete plan under \"plan\"\n14: \n15: **Output format (JSON):**\n16: \n17: ```json\n18: {\n19:   \"questions\": [\n20:     {\"question\": \"What color should the UI element be?\", \"answer\": \"\"},\n21:     {\"question\": \"Should this work offline?\", \"answer\": \"\"}\n22:   ],\n23:   \"plan\": \"Your detailed plan here...\"\n24: }\n25: ```\n26: \n27: **Instructions:**\n28: - Only include \"questions\" if you genuinely need human input to proceed\n29: - If \"questions\" is empty or missing, the plan will be considered complete\n30: - Keep questions specific and actionable\n31: - Write a complete, detailed plan in the \"plan\" field\n32: \n33: Start now and output only valid JSON.\n34: \n35: \n36: ## Previous Review Feedback (you MUST address these issues):\n37: - 2026-03-06T20:49Z | IDEAS | Idea created\n38: - 2026-03-06T22:28Z | PROMOTED | Moved from ideas to plan-inbox\n\n(End of file - total 38 lines)\n</content>","title":".tmp/add-code-path-to-board.instructions","metadata":{"preview":"# Design Planning: add code path to board\n\n**Description:** Add a code path and context file to each board's configuration so that AI agents know where the associated project code lives and have access to project-level context whenever they are invoked. A board lives inside the project it represents (e.g., ~/mycode/.mad/boards/myboard), so the root code path is derivable, but it should be made explicit. Two additions: (1) a `code_path` field in ~/.mad/config.json pointing to the project root, and (2) a ~/.mad/CONTEXT.md file for free-form project context. Agents should also be started with their working directory set to the project root, not the individual work item directory. Every time an agent is invoked, its instructions should include the code path and the path to CONTEXT.md at the top.\n\n---\n\nYou are an AI helping plan this feature. Generate a plan based on the description.\n\n**Your task:**\n1. Analyze the feature description\n2. Identify any unclear points or areas needing clarification\n3. If you have questions for the human, list them in a JSON array under \"questions\"\n4. If you have enough info, write a complete plan under \"plan\"\n\n**Output format (JSON):**\n\n```json\n{\n  \"questions\": [\n    {\"question\": \"What color should the UI element be?\", \"answer\": \"\"},","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1772836376301,"end":1772836376312}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The user wants me to read a file and follow its instructions. Let me first read the file to see what it contains.","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":"e22c37075a3031e5ccb574d2e7dc3554a3598c5f7827e63a0b32109377a2200a"}]}}}}
